  "description": "The current Layer\u202f3 configuration sets the ACL log timer to\u202f300\u202fseconds, with IPv4 class\u2011based ACLs enabled. The system is instructed not to drop packets with the DF flag, but to drop IPv4 fragments; dynamic routing for IPv4 is disabled while IPv6 dynamic routing remains enabled. External loopback interfaces are turned on, yet forwarding of ICMP fragments is turned off. The ICMP generation rate threshold is configured at\u202f1500\u202fpackets per second, and implicit ACL allowance is enabled.\n\nAdditional settings include disabling MIP round\u2011robin, enabling NAT override, and keeping source NAT disabled. TCP/UDP tunnel PMTU handling without an established connection is enabled, and the USIP server is set to discard stray packets.",
